{
  "an10.86:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 10.86 ",
  "an10.86:0.2": "9. Senior Mendicants ",
  "an10.86:0.3": "Overestimation ",
  "an10.86:1.1": "At one time Venerable Mahākassapa was staying near Rājagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the squirrels’ feeding ground. ",
  "an10.86:1.2": "There he addressed the mendicants: ",
  "an10.86:1.3": "“Reverends, mendicants!” ",
  "an10.86:1.4": "“Reverend,” they replied. ",
  "an10.86:1.5": "Venerable Mahākassapa said this: ",
  "an10.86:2.1": "“Take a mendicant who declares enlightenment: ",
  "an10.86:2.2": "‘I understand: “Rebirth is ended, the spiritual journey has been completed, what had to be done has been done, there is nothing further for this place.”’ ",
  "an10.86:2.3": "They’re pursued, pressed, and grilled by the Realized One, or by one of his disciples who has the absorptions, and is skilled in attainments, in the minds of others, and in encompassing another’s mind. ",
  "an10.86:2.4": "Grilled in this way they get stuck or lose their way. They fall to ruin and disaster. ",
  "an10.86:3.1": "The Realized One or one of his disciples encompasses their mind and investigates: ",
  "an10.86:3.2": "‘Why does this venerable declare enlightenment, saying, ",
  "an10.86:3.3": "“I understand: ‘Rebirth is ended, the spiritual journey has been completed, what had to be done has been done, there is nothing further for this place’”?’ ",
  "an10.86:4.1": "They understand, ",
  "an10.86:5.1": "‘This venerable overestimates themselves and tak